# Claims Module — Architecture & Tech Stack
DICEUS Fullstack Assessment v1.0 | .NET 9 + Angular 18 | Greenfield standalone

## Spec hierarchy (source of truth)

1. `Claims_Module_Candidate_Specification.md` (FRS) — business rules, API §10, UI §11, database §6–8
2. `DICEUS_Fullstack_Technical_Assessment.md` — deliverables, evaluation, general stack
3. `.cursor/rules/01-architecture.mdc` through `05-frontend.mdc` — implementation guidance for agents
4. Application code

**On conflict:** FRS wins over Assessment. See **Assessment deviations** in `02-domain.mdc` for known Assessment errors (do not implement those items).

## Solution Projects (MANDATORY STRUCTURE)
- `ClaimsModule.Domain` — entities, value objects, domain events, enumerations. ZERO external dependencies.
- `ClaimsModule.Application` — MediatR commands/queries, FluentValidation validators, DTOs, interfaces, AutoMapper profiles
- `ClaimsModule.Infrastructure` — Azure Blob, Hangfire job implementations, external services
- `ClaimsModule.Persistence` — EF Core DbContext, migrations, repositories, Unit of Work
- `ClaimsModule.API` — ASP.NET Core controllers, middleware, Swagger, startup
- `claims-module-ui/` — Angular 18 project

## Required Tech Stack
| Layer | Package |
|---|---|
| CQRS | MediatR 12+ |
| ORM | Entity Framework Core 9 |
| Validation | FluentValidation — wired at MediatR PIPELINE level, NOT at controller |
| Mapping | AutoMapper — profiles in Application layer ONLY, never in API |
| Background Jobs | Hangfire |
| Database | SQL Server 2022 / Azure SQL |
| File Storage | Azure Blob Storage via IStorageService interface |
| Frontend UI | Angular Material |
| Forms | Reactive Forms only |

## CQRS Rules (Reviewers specifically check this)
- Every state-changing operation = `Command` (e.g. `CreateClaimCommand`, `ApproveReserveCommand`)
- Every read = `Query` (e.g. `GetClaimDetailQuery`, `ListClaimsQuery`)
- Commands and Queries dispatched via `_mediator.Send()`
- Domain Events raised for: `ClaimCreatedEvent`, `ClaimStatusChangedEvent`, `ReserveApprovedEvent`, `ReserveRejectedEvent`, `DocumentUploadedEvent`
- FluentValidation registered as `IPipelineBehavior<TRequest, TResponse>` in MediatR pipeline

## Clean Architecture Rules
- Domain has NO dependencies on any other layer
- Application depends ONLY on Domain
- Infrastructure implements Application interfaces
- Persistence implements Application data-access abstractions via `IClaimsDbContext` + `UnitOfWork` (dedicated `IRepository<T>` interfaces are optional, not required)
- API sends MediatR commands/queries — no business logic in controllers
- AutoMapper profiles NEVER in API layer — always in Application
- Unit of Work wraps multi-table writes in ONE transaction

## Key Interfaces
- `IStorageService` → `AzureBlobStorageService` + `LocalFileSystemStorageService`
- `IAuditLogService` → all audit writes go through this; no direct DbContext writes from handlers
- `ICurrentUserService` → provides current UserId and Role to handlers
- Storage provider configured via `appsettings.json`: `StorageProvider: AzureBlob | LocalFileSystem`

## Error Responses (ALL validation errors use this structure)
```json
{
  "type": "ValidationError",
  "title": "One or more validation errors occurred.",
  "status": 422,
  "errors": { "FieldName": ["Error message."] }
}
```

## Azure Deployment (Required)
- Backend: Azure App Service **or** Azure Container Apps (Assessment §2.3)
- Frontend: Azure Static Web App or App Service
- Azure SQL Database + Azure Blob Storage account
- Azure Key Vault (optional but valued by reviewers)
- CI/CD: GitHub Actions or Azure DevOps — must build + migrate + deploy both

## Deliverables (all required for submission)
- Git repo with full backend + frontend
- EF Core migration files + seed scripts
- `docker-compose.yml` (valued)
- GitHub Actions YAML
- `README.md`, `ARCHITECTURE.md`, `AI-WORKFLOW.md`
- Deployed Swagger URL + deployed frontend URL
- Test credentials: handler role + supervisor role
